g firms, shows Shapiro ahead by roughly 20 to 30 points, and betting markets price his reelection near 97 to 98 percent. With all major raters calling the race Safe or Solid Democratic, the remaining question is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "watch": "A late-breaking scandal or major external event could tighten the race, but no current evidence points to one.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Josh Shapiro, a first-term Democrat in a state that leans slightly Republican, faces Republican nominee Stacy Garrity and Libertarian Ken Krawchuk. Polling since midsummer has been strikingly consistent: every survey, including those from Republican-leaning pollsters, shows Shapiro ahead, with recent leads ranging from roughly 19 to 30 points and an average near 24. Betting markets put his win probability at 97 to 98 percent.\n\nEvery major race rater labels the contest Solid or Safe Democratic. Garrity, backed by a Trump endorsement, has debated Shapiro on tariffs, taxes, health care and abortion, but no public poll shows the race within single digits. Some down-ballot Pennsylvania Republicans are even tying themselves to Shapiro, a sign of his cross-party appeal. The main open question is the size of the margin, not the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9958, "ma